d forwarded it to the  pentagon to put the sensors  onto me so you know it's unfortunate i  think a lot of that stuff  tends to play out behind the scenes and  in my case i felt very passionate about  this project and  didn't feel that i should be bullied in  stepping away from it i thought there  and i still believe there's a lot of  information in this book that is recent  relevant and important for americans to  read about  like what really happens behind the  scenes what it's really like to be in  the room with president trump or  vice president pence or secretary pompeo  like these are  individuals of course who are still in  their respective roles today  you can read for yourself what it's like  to be in those meetings and make a  an educated judgment on whether you like  the direction that we're going or you  think there needs to be a change  yes and many of those descriptions are  fascinating to read we've been talking  with guy snodgrass who is not just a  retired american naval aviator who  served as jim mattis speechwriter and  chief of communications  he also wrote the book holding the line  inside trump's pentagon with secretary  mattis guy really appreciate your time  and and uh  you telling us about not only the  process but about uh your time  uh working with jim mattis thank you so  much yeah thanks david thanks for having  me
 

